@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic surreal body horror, photorealistic
$host = __bh_host__
$room = __bh_room__
$first = {the wrist|the collarbone|the knuckles of one hand}
$ending = {a final tiny crack advances a few millimetres beneath one eye, and HOST becomes even more still|HOST exhales, and a delicate web of hairline cracks blooms across the chest and stops|a single fragment the size of a fingernail slips from the cheek and falls, ringing like a small bell on the floor}

CAST
HOST (image 1): $host

SHOT 10s | push in, slow
HOST stands facing the camera in $room, framed from the waist up, moving naturally. A subtle stiffness begins in the neck: HOST turns the head and it stops almost instantly, with unusual precision. HOST raises one hand; the fingers settle into exact angles, each small adjustment producing a faint crystalline tension. HOST rotates carefully, and a fine hairline fracture appears across the skin near $first and travels a few centimetres before stopping. HOST notices it and becomes extremely careful, lowering the arm with slow controlled movement. Each breath now barely lifts the chest. A thin fracture forms at the temple and branches slowly across the cheek in a beautiful pattern, dividing into finer lines around the jaw. HOST freezes. Only the eyes move, toward the camera. In the final moment $ending.
SFX: quiet room ambience; shallow careful breathing; delicate crystalline tension; tiny high-pitched crackling as each fracture travels
MUSIC: N/A
